# Line endings are part of the contract, not a local convention.
#
# The mutation anchors in `scripts/*_gate_selfcheck.py` compare WORKING-TREE BYTES, so a
# checkout that rewrites LF to CRLF makes every multi-line anchor unmatchable and the
# self-checks report MUTATION_NOT_APPLIED -- a broken-looking harness rather than a newline.
# With `core.autocrlf=true` and no attribute file that is exactly what a fresh checkout on
# Windows produced, and it was hit four times during the rebuild, each time diagnosed as a
# mystery before being recognised.
#
# It was measured, not assumed: a fresh worktree at 1961a92 gave "2 failed, 545 passed"
# (`test_mutation_anchors` LF and anchor-match checks), while the same revision normalised to
# LF gives "547 passed". A repository whose evidence instruments only work in the byte state
# of whoever edited the file last is not reproducible, so the state is declared here.
#
# The index is already LF throughout, so this changes no stored blob and only pins what a
# checkout materialises.
* text=auto eol=lf
